{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162638-pentex-and-the-wyrm-in-werewolf-the-forsaken","id":162638,"title":"Pentex and the Wyrm in Werewolf the Forsaken?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-08T13:13:51-07:00","id":162638,"title":"Pentex and the Wyrm in Werewolf the Forsaken?","content":"Looking for ideas on how to incorporate Pentex and possibly the Wrym into Werewolf the Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/500-rindel","name":"Rindel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T13:34:51-07:00","id":162655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rindel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162638-pentex-and-the-wyrm-in-werewolf-the-forsaken#post162638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Looking for ideas on how to incorporate Pentex and possibly the Wrym into Werewolf the Forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf Translation Guide for starters. Once you read through that, take a look at <i>Hunter: the Vigil</i> \u2014 there is an entire group in there that is basically Pentex with the serial numbers filed off. <i>Spirit Slayers</i>, from that line, can give you more ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T13:59:52-07:00","id":162680,"title":"","content":"It all depends on how much of Apocalypse cosmology you want to import. Can you clarify this a bit, please?<br /> <br /> Because using the Wyrm in a universe with no Wyld and Weaver to counterbalance it (not to mention Gaia) makes thing really easy for the Devourer, since there's no force able to to fight its many, many agents in a effective way if you keep the conflict among Forsaken and Pure. I would probably go with a world with the whole Triat, a silent and unreachable Gaia (no Kami whatsoever) and keep Forsaken's Father Wolf and Mother Luna, but I'd prefer to know what exactly are you looking for before elaborating on things different from what you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T14:22:21-07:00","id":162697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162638-pentex-and-the-wyrm-in-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=162680#post162680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It all depends on how much of Apocalypse cosmology you want to import. Can you clarify this a bit, please?<br /> <br /> Because using the Wyrm in a universe with no Wyld and Weaver to counterbalance it (not to mention Gaia) makes thing really easy for the Devourer, since there's no force able to to fight its many, many agents in a effective way if you keep the conflict among Forsaken and Pure. I would probably go with a world with the whole Triat, a silent and unreachable Gaia (no Kami whatsoever) and keep Forsaken's Father Wolf and Mother Luna, but I'd prefer to know what exactly are you looking for before elaborating on things different from what you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Always liked Pentex in Apocalypse for it's antagonists such as first teams and the Wyrm for such things as Nexus Crawlers and Black Spiral Dancers. So I think I'm basically looking for new antagonists. Would it be possible to have the Wyrm linked to the Bale Hounds in some way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/500-rindel","name":"Rindel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T15:01:52-07:00","id":162744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rindel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162638-pentex-and-the-wyrm-in-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=162697#post162697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Always liked Pentex in Apocalypse for it's antagonists such as first teams and the Wyrm for such things as Nexus Crawlers and Black Spiral Dancers. So I think I'm basically looking for new antagonists. Would it be possible to have the Wyrm linked to the Bale Hounds in some way?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's practically a given. After all, they work for the Maeljin, the entities that were the Wyrm's lieutenants in Apocalypse. They would be more focused, coordinated and a little less prone to infighting with the Heads of the Wyrm behind them.<br /> <br /> In this setting, considering the absence of Apocalypse's regional tribes, the Bale Hounds would be the Black Spiral Dancers for all the needed purposes. Basically, the Bale Hounds would be a lot more, be more aggressive and a major faction that does not hide anymore. You would have a three-sided war between Forsaken, Pure (who have their own ways to deal with the Wyrm, thank you very much) and the Bale Hounds.<br /> <br /> You would have to decide where the line between a negative spirit and a Bane stands, since Forsaken spirits tend to be more amoral than Apocalypse's. Call the Claimed born from this spirits Fomori, and you're done.<br /> <br /> As for Pentex, you can import it easily. The Cheiron Group from Hunter shares indeed some aspects with it, but it can be transplanted into Forsaken without much problem. Perhaps tone down the ecological aspect a bit, since that does not belong to Forsaken as much as it does with Apocalypse<br /> <br /> Edit: the Translation Guide has some tips on how to do this, if I'm not mistaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 06-08-2014, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T15:26:05-07:00","id":162765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162638-pentex-and-the-wyrm-in-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=162744#post162744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Pentex, you can import it easily. The Cheiron Group from Hunter shares indeed some aspects with it, but it can be transplanted into Forsaken without much problem. Perhaps tone down the ecological aspect a bit, since that does not belong to Forsaken as much as it does with Apocalypse<br /> <br /> Edit: the Translation Guide has some tips on how to do this, if I'm not mistaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cheiron was my first thought as well but realized that it needs a quite a bit of tweaking on part of it's ethos to make it work. It's agenda as it currently stands is to make money of the backs of the supernatural. Same with Last Dynasty International (though the Deva corp is a bit different as it exists as a font for the God-Machine but the humans who run it are mostly in it for the money/power). <br /> <br /> If you really want to have things become interesting, I would drop Pentex as is along with the Cheiron Group, Last Dynasty, and Deva for a nice game about corporate warfare slugfest.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T15:34:07-07:00","id":162778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162638-pentex-and-the-wyrm-in-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=162765#post162765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cheiron was my first thought as well but realized that it needs a quite a bit of tweaking on part of it's ethos to make it work. It's agenda as it currently stands is to make money of the backs of the supernatural. Same with Last Dynasty International (though the Deva corp is a bit different as it exists as a font for the God-Machine but the humans who run it are mostly in it for the money/power).<br /> <br /> If you really want to have things become interesting, I would drop Pentex as is along with the Cheiron Group, Last Dynasty, and Deva for a nice game about corporate warfare slugfest.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree. Cheiron it's similar to Pentex in some ways but, instead of having a Pentex clone that differs too much from the original where it really matters, it's probably better to directly use the real deal.<br /> <br /> And yes, having Pentex in the same universe of Cheiron, Deva and Last Dinasty seems really fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T15:37:58-07:00","id":162789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162638-pentex-and-the-wyrm-in-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=162680#post162680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It all depends on how much of Apocalypse cosmology you want to import. Can you clarify this a bit, please?<br /> <br /> Because using the Wyrm in a universe with no Wyld and Weaver to counterbalance it (not to mention Gaia) makes thing really easy for the Devourer, since there's no force able to to fight its many, many agents in a effective way if you keep the conflict among Forsaken and Pure. I would probably go with a world with the whole Triat, a silent and unreachable Gaia (no Kami whatsoever) and keep Forsaken's Father Wolf and Mother Luna, but I'd prefer to know what exactly are you looking for before elaborating on things different from what you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weaver = God-Machine?<br /> Wyld=Principle?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Or Wyld = Wyrd and faes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T16:32:04-07:00","id":162905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162638-pentex-and-the-wyrm-in-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=162778#post162778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I completely agree. Cheiron it's similar to Pentex in some ways but, instead of having a Pentex clone that differs too much from the original where it really matters, it's probably better to directly use the real deal.<br /> <br /> And yes, having Pentex in the same universe of Cheiron, Deva and Last Dinasty seems really fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be but as some people already brought up, there are some cosmology issues with importing Pentex. Using the Maeljin could work but the Maeljin in nWoD aren't so much environmentally destructive as they are corruptive in general in spreading their influence.<br /> <br /> This could be worked around via re-conning the Wyrm as an old enemy that Father Wolf put down and made slumber (Why he didn't throw it up on the Luna with the Moon-Banished could be anyone's guess but meh) and the Mealjin were it's servants. Given the fact that the world is progressively getting crappier, the Mealjin finally gathered enough power to start engaging their plan to free the Wyrm from it's slumber and make the world more of a festering hell hole than it already is.<br /> <br /> The purposeful environmental degradation of Pentex is now part of a ritual to awaken the Wyrm from it's slumber so it will be now an active spirit (on par with Luna or even the God-Machine) and proceed to rampage across the world.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T16:37:53-07:00","id":162910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162638-pentex-and-the-wyrm-in-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=162765#post162765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cheiron was my first thought as well but realized that it needs a quite a bit of tweaking on part of it's ethos to make it work. It's agenda as it currently stands is to make money of the backs of the supernatural. Same with Last Dynasty International (though the Deva corp is a bit different as it exists as a font for the God-Machine but the humans who run it are mostly in it for the money/power).<br /> <br /> If you really want to have things become interesting, I would drop Pentex as is along with the Cheiron Group, Last Dynasty, and Deva for a nice game about corporate warfare slugfest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pentex (or, properly speaking, Magadon Inc) has a tremendous advantage over Cheiron in that it doesn't need to go looking for spare parts. It makes them, in quantities far greater than Cheiron could manage without heavy casualties to its collection agents. What's more, if the collection agents were to try poaching some of their stuff, it would likely stand a good chance of turning Cheiron agents from the inside out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T16:57:43-07:00","id":162963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162638-pentex-and-the-wyrm-in-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=162910#post162910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pentex (or, properly speaking, Magadon Inc) has a tremendous advantage over Cheiron in that it doesn't need to go looking for spare parts. It makes them, in quantities far greater than Cheiron could manage without heavy casualties to its collection agents. What's more, if the collection agents were to try poaching some of their stuff, it would likely stand a good chance of turning Cheiron agents from the inside out.</div> </div> </div> </div>On a 1:1 fight, you are most likely correct. However, I suspect that Cheiron is a bit more &quot;market aware&quot; than Pentex given that Cheiron isn't trying to put an agenda over profit. Same with the other companies that will fight each other for market share.<br /> <br /> I can easily see other companies attacking Pentex on it's environmental record and using national regulations and like to hammer it out of certain markets.<br /> <br /> edit:<br /> <br /> To expand on this, Pentex would be akin to a megacorp version of Walmart when it comes to pharm while Cheiron would be a bit more focused and thus being able to carve out market niches that Pentex simply can't reach. Likewise with other companies. I also suspect that Cheiron, given that it can't produce it's own army which it can then cannibalize, has a bigger R&amp;D department that it can leverage to be more...creative with it's product line and thus being able to pass on the benefits to it's procurement teams.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 06-08-2014, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T17:28:33-07:00","id":162988,"title":"","content":"Pentex kind of works off of a handwaving of resources, though. Every subsidiary is the top of its field, and they control everything from politicians and small governments to the actual activists and groups protesting their actions.<br /> <br /> Dropping them in, especially as a competitor to Cheiron, which is a great company but, as in the rest of the World of Darkness, not one that is as over-the-top, or omniscient, would result in two 'top of the line' companies (though really we'd be talking about Magadon, the Pentex subsidiary which is a more accurate analog to Cheiron than the massive Pentex), one of whom is working on new World of Darkness principles where they have to work in between the lines, and the other working off of the fact that a cosmic force of corruption rewards them for doing their job, whether they are profitable or not.<br /> <br /> Bringing the Wyrm (or any aspect of the game) over is doable, but the more extreme elements of classic World of Darkness would blow the more subtle or down-to-earth (realistic doesn't quite fit) aspects of new World of Darkness out of the water.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T17:40:01-07:00","id":162997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162638-pentex-and-the-wyrm-in-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=162988#post162988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bringing the Wyrm (or any aspect of the game) over is doable, but the more extreme elements of classic World of Darkness would blow the more subtle or down-to-earth (realistic doesn't quite fit) aspects of new World of Darkness out of the water.</div> </div> </div> </div>That and perhaps look at Shadowrun for inspiration.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T17:50:31-07:00","id":163009,"title":"","content":"I suppose I should have said, adding the Wyrm as is.<br /> <br /> If you wanted to bring it over to fit the more subtle world of Forsaken, you'd want to really decide what it is. In the new World of Darkness, spirits are spirits, they aren't inherently bad or inherently good, and they mostly act as reflections of real world things. Spirits of murder don't just pop into being and start inducing people to kill others. They come into being because something, likely murder, created them. Spirits of death, decay, even disease aren't evil things, they're entirely natural, and part of the spiritual aspect of Forsaken is accepting that and recognizing that getting rid of things like death and disease can have as bad consequences as getting rid of spirits of life and medicine. <br /> <br /> So you'd want to figure out where things like Wyrm-taint started or stopped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T18:20:15-07:00","id":163033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162638-pentex-and-the-wyrm-in-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=162963#post162963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On a 1:1 fight, you are most likely correct. However, I suspect that Cheiron is a bit more &quot;market aware&quot; than Pentex given that Cheiron isn't trying to put an agenda over profit. Same with the other companies that will fight each other for market share.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pentex's agenda is profit over everything else. That's why they skimp on expensive maintenance of oil tankers. That's why they stop at nothing to crush their competitors. The fact that spiritual corruption dovetails so nicely into no holds barred capitalism is part of W:TA's takedown of modern capitalism - nothing needs to be done on their part more than keep on grinding everything down because they can make huge profits off of it. The monsters are only around to provide a distraction and security measure against the monsters that would do something about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I can easily see other companies attacking Pentex on it's environmental record and using national regulations and like to hammer it out of certain markets. </div> </div> </div>Given how well that works in the real world? Not really, no. They'd get branded &quot;green freaks&quot; by Pentex PR, who offers many more all-important jobs and manages to convince everyone that it's saving the world. Because jobs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> edit:<br /> <br /> To expand on this, Pentex would be akin to a megacorp version of Walmart when it comes to pharm while Cheiron would be a bit more focused and thus being able to carve out market niches that Pentex simply can't reach. Likewise with other companies. I also suspect that Cheiron, given that it can't produce it's own army which it can then cannibalize, has a bigger R&amp;D department that it can leverage to be more...creative with it's product line and thus being able to pass on the benefits to it's procurement teams. </div> </div> </div>Pentex has its own names changed to protect the guilty version of Walmart. And all the other companies that the Subsidiaries represent. Cheiron would be going head to head against Magadon... and it would frequently end up with black eyes, because it doesn't have the support that Magadon does, and it doesn't act as a chemical weapons supplier. Which could, say, be used in a false flag operation to &quot;expose&quot; how Cheiron is doing dirty work for warmongers when a nerve gas accident takes out an important research site. Several of them. In a row. Oh, what a poor day for Cheiron.<br /> <br /> &quot;No!&quot; Cheiron yelled. &quot;I must defeat the Pentex!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;No,&quot; said the market analysts. &quot;Cheiron, you are the Pentex.&quot;<br /> <br /> And then Cheiron was a subsidiary. Because it was eaten by Magadon, who kindly offered to soak up the costs of cleaning up all the &quot;accident sites&quot; that the company left behind. No one pays attention, the world continues turning in a downward spiral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T18:42:59-07:00","id":163042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162638-pentex-and-the-wyrm-in-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=163033#post163033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pentex's agenda is profit over everything else. That's why they skimp on expensive maintenance of oil tankers. </div> </div> </div> </div>That's more because if oil tankers spill, Endron and Pentex profits in other ways.<br /> <br /> Also, Cheiron isn't a champion for Gaia, Cheiron hunts for profit. They have no reason to fight Pentex. Especially when, as long as Pentex is active, they can just snatch the occasional formori and make some profit taking it apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-08-2014, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T18:50:34-07:00","id":163046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162638-pentex-and-the-wyrm-in-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=163033#post163033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pentex has its own names changed to protect the guilty version of Walmart. And all the other companies that the Subsidiaries represent. Cheiron would be going head to head against Magadon... and it would frequently end up with black eyes, because it doesn't have the support that Magadon does, and it doesn't act as a chemical weapons supplier. Which could, say, be used in a false flag operation to &quot;expose&quot; how Cheiron is doing dirty work for warmongers when a nerve gas accident takes out an important research site. Several of them. In a row. Oh, what a poor day for Cheiron.<br /> <br /> &quot;No!&quot; Cheiron yelled. &quot;I must defeat the Pentex!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;No,&quot; said the market analysts. &quot;Cheiron, you are the Pentex.&quot;<br /> <br /> And then Cheiron was a subsidiary. Because it was eaten by Magadon, who kindly offered to soak up the costs of cleaning up all the &quot;accident sites&quot; that the company left behind. No one pays attention, the world continues turning in a downward spiral.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then, the God-Machine noticed something odd, hit the rest function and now we are right back where we started <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I have a feeling that this is less of how to include Pentex in nWoD and more of a proxy &quot;My World of Darkness is better than yours!&quot;. In which case, I have to agree with nofather, neutering certain parts of Pentex would be good to make it more realistic would be best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 06-08-2014, 09:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T18:52:33-07:00","id":163047,"title":"","content":"Leaving Pentex aside for a moment, I'd propose that the Wyrm is an ancient, ancient spirit-thing, not unlike the Idigam, that can corrupt spirits. Wyrm-taint is literal corrupted essence. A murder-spirit may not be a Wyrmspirit, but it's a prime candidate to become one. Wyrm-spirits don't seek to cause destruction too feed their Essence, and grow stronger, it'd be a literal madness that is horrendous to spirits. It'd cause them to go made, growing into wanton destruction, and corruption because it's unnatural. Some spirits will burn out of Essence and strength when tainted, but others will grow and thrive, gaining bans, banes and Influences related to their new.... lifestyle. Those are the dangerous ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T18:55:31-07:00","id":163049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162638-pentex-and-the-wyrm-in-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=163047#post163047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leaving Pentex aside for a moment, I'd propose that the Wyrm is an ancient, ancient spirit-thing, not unlike the Idigam, that can corrupt spirits. Wyrm-taint is literal corrupted essence. A murder-spirit may not be a Wyrmspirit, but it's a prime candidate to become one. Wyrm-spirits don't seek to cause destruction too feed their Essence, and grow stronger, it'd be a literal madness that is horrendous to spirits. It'd cause them to go made, growing into wanton destruction, and corruption because it's unnatural. Some spirits will burn out of Essence and strength when tainted, but others will grow and thrive, gaining bans, banes and Influences related to their new.... lifestyle. Those are the dangerous ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>So an Infernal Archdemon? Most likely rank 9 (reserve rank 10 for the big man himself)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T18:57:31-07:00","id":163050,"title":"","content":"That might actually dovetail with Inferno's rank 10 Adversary. Inferno offers the idea of diaboli, a type of demon that has been created by spirits merging with or being corrupted by other demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T18:58:39-07:00","id":163051,"title":"","content":"That's about what I had in mind. In my game the Wyrm exists as an ancient spirit who was outcast to the Lower Depths. It's taint spreads among Wounds. It can, basically, turn spirits into Dominions (I think that's the name from Inferno) rather easily. Now, I wouldn't say you have to tie the Wyrm into Inferno, but it's a nice handy way to do so. I'd also suggest using the Claimed instead of the Possessed, but perhaps allow the Claimed to get Vestments?<br /> <br /> Anyways, it hasn't come up in my campaign as of yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T19:03:34-07:00","id":163055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162638-pentex-and-the-wyrm-in-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=163050#post163050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That might actually dovetail with Inferno's rank 10 Adversary. Inferno offers the idea of diaboli, a type of demon that has been created by spirits merging with or being corrupted by other demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I say rank 9 mostly due to the fact that the Inferno has it's fingers everywhere (Astral, Shadow, Twilight, Material, perhaps even the Underworld) and the Wyrm as it would primarily be focused on the Shadow. If we are using the Adversary, I would view of a being of that rank of being able to be cross purpose and extremely powerful in all worlds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162638-pentex-and-the-wyrm-in-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=163051#post163051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's about what I had in mind. In my game the Wyrm exists as an ancient spirit who was outcast to the Lower Depths. It's taint spreads among Wounds. It can, basically, turn spirits into Dominions (I think that's the name from Inferno) rather easily. Now, I wouldn't say you have to tie the Wyrm into Inferno, but it's a nice handy way to do so. I'd also suggest using the Claimed instead of the Possessed, but perhaps allow the Claimed to get Vestments?<br /> <br /> Anyways, it hasn't come up in my campaign as of yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Infernal demons in my game lose the ability to claim in favor of the Supreme Possession trait which I always thought was more in theme of Infernal demons than just outright claiming them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 06-08-2014, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T21:11:38-07:00","id":163112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rindel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162638-pentex-and-the-wyrm-in-werewolf-the-forsaken#post162638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Looking for ideas on how to incorporate Pentex and possibly the Wrym into Werewolf the Forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here is the problem with the wyrm in NWoD. In OWoD the Wyrm was supposed to Shiva , the destroyer or entropy playing off Wyld's creation and Weaver's (pattern) order.<br /> Pattern restrained the Wyrm which drove it insane. Which in turn turned it into the corrupting force it was known as in the OWoD darkness.<br /> You can't have the the corruped Wyrm without the out of control Weaver or Pattern.<br /> <br /> Seems to me Pentext 2.0 should be a front for Majelian or Abyssals if that is at all possible.<br /> <br /> Your milage may vary. BTW look at the Idigam chronicle development.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T22:46:13-07:00","id":163183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162638-pentex-and-the-wyrm-in-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=163033#post163033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;No!&quot; Cheiron yelled. &quot;I must defeat the Pentex!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;No,&quot; said the market analysts. &quot;Cheiron, you are the Pentex.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have much to add to this conversation-I own Apocalypse but I'm far from an expert-but I imagine the conversation goes something like this, actually:<br /> <br /> &quot;We'll make this simple Pentex. You might be larger, have greater ease of production, sure. But within the next five years, you will either merge with us or be defeated by us.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Ha. We'll have the world burning by then&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;We've been through that already. I hope you have other cards to play&quot;<br /> <br /> (For context, in Compacts and Conspiracies, a major theory is provided saying the Board of Directors are actualy mega aliens that survived the end of one world and are here to do more-either end it again or save it)l","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T23:01:09-07:00","id":163212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162638-pentex-and-the-wyrm-in-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=163183#post163183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (For context, in Compacts and Conspiracies, a major theory is provided saying the Board of Directors are actualy mega aliens that survived the end of one world and are here to do more-either end it again or save it)l</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, my first thought is that the Cheiron BoD is the same as the Pentex board, and they just survived the destruction of the Old world, into the New world. xD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T23:13:01-07:00","id":163216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162638-pentex-and-the-wyrm-in-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=163212#post163212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, my first thought is that the Cheiron BoD is the same as the Pentex board, and they just survived the destruction of the Old world, into the New world. xD</div> </div> </div> </div>Br said the same thing. I just find that to be a reason they'd laugh at Pentex all the more.<br /> <br /> Whether or not they can afford those laughs is a question I won't bother with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T03:15:12-07:00","id":163347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162638-pentex-and-the-wyrm-in-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=163183#post163183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have much to add to this conversation-I own Apocalypse but I'm far from an expert-but I imagine the conversation goes something like this, actually:<br /> <br /> &quot;We'll make this simple Pentex. You might be larger, have greater ease of production, sure. But within the next five years, you will either merge with us or be defeated by us.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Ha. We'll have the world burning by then&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;We've been through that already. I hope you have other cards to play&quot;<br /> <br /> (For context, in Compacts and Conspiracies, a major theory is provided saying the Board of Directors are actualy mega aliens that survived the end of one world and are here to do more-either end it again or save it)l</div> </div> </div> </div>It's always irked me that theory was presented as &quot;The truth&quot; in C&amp;C. Cheiron in my mind began back in Ancient Greece where a mortal found a way to codify Pyros to the point where they can slap bits of supernaturals on to mortals and started calling a few friends . Though the ages they prefect the art until you reach the point where you are effectively have &quot;mortals&quot; bashing open vampire and werewolf eldars/True Fae to keep themselves operational and keep their professional curiosity entertained. Fast forward past the Roman Empire, the Middle Ages, the Renaissance (a Major point on Cheiron's history but I don't have time to explain) to the age of empires where Cheiron starts to get more abrasive when it comes getting what it wants. It's soon to be members were majority shareholders in the East India Company which became fabulously wealthy as it basically owned India and several markets by proxy. Following the success of that venture (viewed as a successful distraction by most of the group), Cheiron reinvested back into the medical field with it's most notable accomplishment is giving Louis Pasteur the resources necessary to create the rabies vaccine for mortals (Cheiron figured out it werewolves were immune to most diseases and got a tissue sample for Louis to study).<br /> <br /> From there it was the civil war (something they didn't have a major part in but were there to get samples), to it's official incorporation in 1859. The great war hit them hard in the pocketbook however was international trade was cut off as Europe killed it's young. They had enough assets in the US and various other places to continue on though. However, Cheiron's greatest screw up was the unintentional release of a virus which would be latter be known as Spanish flu by one of it's Hunters who dropped the jar on a troop ship (this is the precursor to the extinction virus that Cheiron holds in the freezer somewhere). Aside from accidentally killing 3% to 5% of the world's population, They road the highs of the 20s, survived the 30s, and through government contracts, continued through the 40s. It's in the 50s that they began to gain public momentum. That continues to snowball into present day where they have a size able hold (if not outright monopoly) on several markets in the medical field via it's patents.<br /> <br /> Of course that is simplifying my head cannon a bit when it comes to them and I've left out several projects which blew up in their faces (sometimes literally) but simply put, I've always had the idea of Cheiron of being a bit more interesting that just &quot;We're aliens who fucked up our own planet&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":". 06-09-2014, 06:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T03:24:21-07:00","id":163349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dreaminggod</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162638-pentex-and-the-wyrm-in-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=163047#post163047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leaving Pentex aside for a moment, I'd propose that the Wyrm is an ancient, ancient spirit-thing, not unlike the Idigam, that can corrupt spirits. Wyrm-taint is literal corrupted essence. A murder-spirit may not be a Wyrmspirit, but it's a prime candidate to become one. Wyrm-spirits don't seek to cause destruction too feed their Essence, and grow stronger, it'd be a literal madness that is horrendous to spirits. It'd cause them to go made, growing into wanton destruction, and corruption because it's unnatural. Some spirits will burn out of Essence and strength when tainted, but others will grow and thrive, gaining bans, banes and Influences related to their new.... lifestyle. Those are the dangerous ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this idea, I'll borrow it if that's okay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/500-rindel","name":"Rindel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T06:06:24-07:00","id":163490,"title":"","content":"Ooh, I have an idea for what Wyrmtaint looks like mechanically (in GMC, anyway.)<br /> <br /> 1. Replace one Dot of Influences with 'Wyrm'<br /> 2. Futz with other Influences to reflect the destructive and polluted nature of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> <b>Example:</b> The Rank 2 Spirit of a small mountain river is ensnared and afflicted with Wyrmtaint. Its Influences are initially Water \u2022\u2022; after it becomes Tainted, the Influences are Polluted Water \u2022 and Wyrm \u2022. It then proceeds to foul up the river so it can feed on the tasty, tasty Essence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T07:18:52-07:00","id":163558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162638-pentex-and-the-wyrm-in-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=163347#post163347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's always irked me that theory was presented as &quot;The truth&quot; in C&amp;C.</div> </div> </div> </div>More like the truth that the writers preferred-remember, mystery is a theme.<br /> <br /> Me, I like it, particularly the idea of them being an alien Vigil from an Earth that failed, but then I've always had a thing for those sorts of stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T09:23:35-07:00","id":163668,"title":"","content":"I honestly see no reason not to include the Weaver, Wyld, and Wyrm As-Is in the new world of darkness, and just have them as slightly more distant forces than they were in oWoD. The Wyrm represents Entropy and (because of a snafu in the nature of reality) Corruption. But instead of falling into the trap of making every &quot;bad&quot; spirit wyrm-tainted, only have the direct influence of the Wyrm show up with the truly corrupt and fucked-up spirits. The wyrm can operate on a much more macro level, such that most people (and even most werewolves) never really encounter its direct servitors, and once you start to you know you're in really, really deep. <br /> <br /> Basically, I see no reason it's strictly <i>necessary </i>to downgrade the Wyrm from &quot;underpinning of the universe&quot; into &quot;something Father Wolf hunted&quot; or &quot;just some really big spirit&quot;. It works fine as it was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T17:31:32-07:00","id":164232,"title":"","content":"I think it'd work doing such. As I said, I haven't decided what the Wyrm is, I've name-dropped him in the First Tongue but it hasn't really come up again. (mostly since that game died.), but I may do something on it because this threads got me thinking. <br /> <br /> On that note, what about the Wyrm being the Lower Depths? I mean, you could make a good case for the Supernal being part, or the whole, Wyld, and the God-Machine makes a good Weaver, but the things below? That sounds like the Wyrm. <br /> <br /> As it is in my game, I have the Wyrm, but haven't really included the Wyld. The Weaver's been cannibalized by the God-Machine in my game, so I won't use more than angels, and Infrastructure. It just extends to the Shadow, Weaver-taint is just Infrastructure in the Shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u><b>My Homebrew</b></u><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1PLu_eTg03h4ogiTSGSkzEB7T_1YpB9_VkhHmgZN41-I/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Star Wars d10</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">T</a><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1rIXZorT7CR5SREkdT3m0zbB3_gwf1484-gUVlG1JnhQ/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">he Fallen for Demon: the Descent</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1-TDr4NF_5cUn-In2vjI9P5LTKqsu9B4-OMxbnbaTgT8/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Requiem for a Masquerade: VtR 2e Cainite Conversion</a> (<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1HpKi5giBNsQrZRLIRRjaCe7sHVm1Q13ravVYlE45Dbw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Vampira Roma</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod","name":"Dreaminggod","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"745"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T19:43:17-07:00","id":164319,"title":"","content":"The more I think about it, The more I start to realize that the Wyrm has the deck very stacked against it in &quot;Default&quot; nWoD.<br /> <br /> Most entites in W:tF will oppose it to the point perhaps uniting the Forsaken, Pure, and maybe even some of the Moon-Banished (even some of the Idigam have agendas which would be disrupted if the world was killed off) along with very powerful spirits.<br /> <br /> The Exarchs and Archmagi would look down to see that the world they depend on is getting thrashed and while the Exarchs are dicks about most things, destroying elements of their oppression would get their attention. Same with the Pentacle.<br /> <br /> Hunter compacts and conspiracies from not only Cheiron but the Lucifuge (assuming the Wyrm is an infernal demon), The Union, Network Zero and more would be very unhappy with a &quot;monster production line&quot; of Pentex.<br /> <br /> Don't know about the Deathlords(going off Raven's vision of them being overworked trying to get everyone to pass on, they may take interest in the world not ending purely to keep their workload manageable and not having the dead walk the earth) but the Judges are like the Exarchs in respect, they want to keep mummy's cults operational and more importantly, keep sending them crap in Duat. Again, something that would be highly inconvenienced with the world ending.<br /> <br /> The Empyrean which was hinted at in WoD: Inferno.<br /> <br /> Elements of the Inferno who don't want the world killed off because they love it (stated outright in the book).<br /> <br /> And then you have the God-Machine who's sole purpose seems to be built on preventing the world from ending and backing it up from saved points every so often when it does (Seattle for instance).<br /> <br /> The wild cards would be the Fae (can't see Arcadia burning from the Wyrm), The Principle (mostly because it does it's own thing because it's the Principle), and maybe the Aeons.<br /> <br /> The Abyss of course would be very happy with the Wyrm for ending the world and thus it's suffering but that's about it.<br /> <br /> This is not to say that the Wyrm can't blow up the default nWoD, it's just gonna have a very, very hard time trying to get pass entities who either benefit from the status quo or who's sole job is preserving it in doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","user":"Shock","date":".  spelling 06-10-2014, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-09T22:56:18-07:00","id":164536,"title":"","content":"I've had the idea in my head for a little while now that Pentex and the subsidiaries are a deal between some clever Bale Hounds and some humans looking for power. Bales give the humans real, physical supernatural abilities by following the bad spirits, and Pentex helps make the world ready for said spirits entrance. The Cheiron angle can simply be observed as a difference in specialization; where Pentex does have a pharma branch, Cheiron's been doing it so well for so long that everyone hits their products as opposed to Pentex's stuff.<br /> <br /> Another thing I've noticed is that Pentex would definitely have more than a little competition from all the other hunters out there who would make for unexpected allies for a wolf pack. Union cells protesting labor practices, Keepers of the Source protesting the environmental record, the Barrett Commission investigating some trading deals, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T07:20:53-07:00","id":164814,"title":"","content":"Hmm, while claimed are the closest to fomori in nwod, I think there would be some problems there: first of all, the spirit claimed can get way too powerful, and the spirit, who is in charge when it comes to claimed, are too monomaniac, they would follow their own natures, not their orders.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest that idea of humans duplicating essence shaping I proposed on the old forum be adapted here. A company discovered essence, and how living things can be mutated by the nature of essence added to it, so the company captures spirits (and maybe ghosts too if you want) and harvests them for essence to add to their operatives.<br /> <br /> So they inject the essence into someone and the person might get stone skin, fire blood, tentacle tongues, snake fangs, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> Even if you didn't include the wyrm in this, this would get the werewolves attention because humans abusing spirits is just as offensive to them as spirits abusing humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-10T08:57:31-07:00","id":164856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162638-pentex-and-the-wyrm-in-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=164814#post164814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Hmm, while claimed are the closest to fomori in nwod, I think there would be some problems there: first of all, the spirit claimed can get way too powerful, and the spirit, who is in charge when it comes to claimed, are too monomaniac, they would follow their own natures, not their orders.<br /> <br /> I'd suggest that idea of humans duplicating essence shaping I proposed on the old forum be adapted here. A company discovered essence, and how living things can be mutated by the nature of essence added to it, so the company captures spirits (and maybe ghosts too if you want) and harvests them for essence to add to their operatives.<br /> <br /> So they inject the essence into someone and the person might get stone skin, fire blood, tentacle tongues, snake fangs, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> Even if you didn't include the wyrm in this, this would get the werewolves attention because humans abusing spirits is just as offensive to them as spirits abusing humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a Mortal infused Fey... Not a changeling, exactly, but very similar is substance, so to speak. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T00:57:47-07:00","id":165715,"title":"","content":"&quot;The Children of the Wyrm&quot; as a hidden, massively powerful sect of spirit-worshippers in a conglomerate sounds like a Hunter Conspiracy to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-11T22:41:16-07:00","id":166640,"title":"","content":"Ooooh, a company that's developed a form of essence shaping. I can definitely truck with that. Les Mysteres was always a bit too much of the &quot;potential victim&quot; angle for me. Humans dabbling in something beyond the for fun and profit fits quite well, and not actively stepping on the toes of Cheiron means they can fit into crossovers well enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-12T22:35:52-07:00","id":167584,"title":"","content":"Yeah it was one of my brainstorming for making bleeding edge games more attune with the other gamelines, so essence shaping plug-ins for werewolf, spoiling based liquid discipline juicers for vampire, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T21:58:55-07:00","id":244534,"title":"","content":"Something that comes with pentex is mockery breeds. We know one of the new ones is where rhinos. Could be fun (or not) for a setting in Africa.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T22:44:59-07:00","id":244555,"title":"","content":"Well if one used the war against the pure shapeshifter rules, then a magically advanced company could theoretically create their own shapeshifters, perhaps as designer babies, or a magical disease if one wanted a technological edge to it, if not it might be a curse or a magical ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T23:13:26-07:00","id":244566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162638-pentex-and-the-wyrm-in-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=244555#post244555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well if one used the war against the pure shapeshifter rules, then a magically advanced company could theoretically create their own shapeshifters, perhaps as designer babies, or a magical disease if one wanted a technological edge to it, if not it might be a curse or a magical ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, Cheiron comes to mind but creating their own pack of shapeshifters doesn't seem like their style. Why put so much investment in a series of products in which the rate of return is greater when you use cheaper augmented field agents?<br /> <br /> But of course, that's implying that Cheiron is planning on fielding these shifters instead of simply farming the poor bastards.<br /> <br /> You could have a nWoD adaption of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Constant_Gardener\" target=\"_blank\"><i>The Constant Gardener</i></a> where Cherion simply rounds up a town in India or Africa, turns them into beasts, and then harvests the crap out of them for medical research.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T00:18:11-07:00","id":244612,"title":"","content":"I think you should know pentex' mindset first on the mockeries. They're at constant war with the werewolves, so they need usable consistently powerful allies to the fera. They have black spiral dancers, but their allegiance only goes so far. Interestingly the person incharge of creating them is a black spiral... But yes it's an alternative to the bsds, not a product but gauranteed allies on par with garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T01:32:04-07:00","id":244673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162638-pentex-and-the-wyrm-in-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=244534#post244534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something that comes with pentex is mockery breeds. We know one of the new ones is where rhinos. Could be fun (or not) for a setting in Africa.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Kerasi are (IMO) awesome. Just sayin'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T01:34:19-07:00","id":244674,"title":"","content":"Can't wait to read about em! How's their viability in a conversion style game? Do they have gift accessibility?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T06:59:48-07:00","id":244776,"title":"","content":"What do you mean by 'conversion style game'? Just trying to work out how to answer this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T07:45:48-07:00","id":244789,"title":"","content":"Cross over stuff from apocalypse to forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T10:19:07-07:00","id":244860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/162638-pentex-and-the-wyrm-in-werewolf-the-forsaken?p=244789#post244789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cross over stuff from apocalypse to forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>Proper term is 'translation' from the eponymous guides, y'know, fyi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T17:23:02-07:00","id":245076,"title":"","content":"Ok, how would they translate to Forsaken? Leaving aside the whole Pentex/Wyrm deal, Kerasi would be pretty easy to transfer. A simple translation would make them twisted science experiments from unethical labs, but I'd probably make them the victims/shock troops of one of the newly returned Idigam, twisting the essence of natural creatures to build its army of shapeshifting monsters to destroy the Uratha.<br /> <br /> (Just a quick answer, of course.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T20:49:24-07:00","id":245160,"title":"","content":"The Werewolf Translation Guide would be enough to do it, I think. Any Kerasi Gifts would be easy. The story elements would need chopping and changing as Bunyip said. Kerasi breeds and auspices (or equivalents) would be slightly harder, but the WTG would help. Any intrinsic kerasi powers would need some Aspect eyeballing maybe.<br /> <br /> Either way, I'd still want to play one just to charge ALL the things. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/167-nikink","name":"nikink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T21:53:59-07:00","id":245184,"title":"","content":"Actually bunyip that's brilliant! Has anyone proposed making the wyrm itself an idigam? I can't recall atm and I'm at work so I can't freely browse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T23:59:06-07:00","id":245209,"title":"","content":"I don't believe they have, but if I was running a game that wanted to draw on Apocalypse, the Wyrm (under a suitably First Tongue name) would be a formless Idigam twisting the essence and purpose of everything it touches, from that first small-but-growing corporation it happened across (Pentex), to the first packs of Uratha who went deep into the bowels of the earth to destroy it (Black Spiral Dancers), to the twisted humans (formori) and the mockery breeds it makes from twisting other natural animals and seeing what happens when it merges them with humans and Uratha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T00:58:12-07:00","id":245217,"title":"","content":"This is good 'new' translation guide stuff. Could do the whole triat as celestial level idigam.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T01:24:18-07:00","id":245232,"title":"","content":"I'll talk to Stew and see what he thinks about writing some kind of web-enhancement doing just that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T08:45:53-07:00","id":245354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\">